[ext_resource type="Resource" path="res://resources/tiles/road_banked_left.tres" id="2_profile"]

; The mirror of CurveRight, and here to prove the mirroring rather than to add a corner: the bank
; has to climb toward the *outside*, which is the side opposite the way the piece turns. A left
; turn throws the car right, so road_banked_left is the profile with BankToLeft off. Getting that
; backwards builds a corner that tips you off it, and it is the first thing to check when one
; drives wrong.
;
; Exit lands at (-63, 0, -63) heading -X, which is what TrackAnchor.Swept gives for side -1.
